Co-creation and active learner involvement are demonstrated to
improve the quality of education as it takes into consideration the
learners needs and it also stimulates the teachers’ growth [8]. It
has also the potential to improve the motivation as the learners
feel engaged and empowered being actively involved in creating
the content [3]. While co-creation tends to be explored or used

